<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yazdegerd III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 651 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yazdegerd III was the last king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>, who came to the throne as a youth in the 630s. His reign saw the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muslim-conquest-of-persia">Arab conquest of Iran</a>, with decisive defeats at al-Qadisiyya and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nahavand">Nahavand</a>. He fled eastwards and was killed near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merv">Merv</a> in 651 CE, an event that marked the end of the Sasanian dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yazdegerd-iii.jpg" alt="Yazdegerd III" width="320" height="306" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group; [1] · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_the_Sasanian_king_Yazdegerd_III,_651_mint_(Cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
